4) Loop relation
Model a loop only if an activity or block repeats within the same case.
- A loop must represent recurring behavior, not noise or accidental label repetition.
- The redo part must represent what can happen again.
- Every loop must allow eventual termination.
- Every loop must include at least one mandatory activity per iteration (no empty iterations).
- When modeling a loop where the same activity repeats, create the activity object once and pass the same reference to both do and redo
- Avoid multiple independent optional loops inside one large partial_order block, because they create state-space explosion.

